From: Mdjavad2nd prf <md.javad01@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:59:06 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] feat(shop): category tree and paginated products for 1800
 items (v1.7.16)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Built on the released 1.7.15, not on the unmerged 1.8.0 series, so this can be
applied on its own.

The shop has more than ten categories and 1800 products. GET /shop/products
answers that by sending everything at once and hydrating every product: roughly
600 KB of JSON and 1800 wc_get_product() calls per request.

Two new endpoints in a file of their own:

- GET /shop/categories — the tree with parent and count, no products. Ten rows,
  under 2 KB, cached in a transient for ten minutes: a warm hit runs zero
  queries. Invalidated on product and category saves.
- GET /shop/catalog?category=&page=&per_page= — one page of one category, 24
  products, with total and totalPages. Subcategories come from WooCommerce's own
  include_children.

Products are chosen by WooCommerce visibility (published, not hidden from the
catalog) rather than a hand-ticked list: 1800 checkboxes is not a workflow.

GET /shop/products is untouched; the web app keeps working.
